{
  "requirement": "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: not satisfied.** The implementation looks correct, but the tests miss two explicit obligations of `requirements.ci.determination`.\n\n**What is implemented and tested**\n- `validate_evidence_file` in `src/evidence.rs` (about lines 637–645) carries the `{impl}` marker. It parses the determination with `Judgment::from_value`.\n- `true` and `{\"FIXME\": [...]}` add no error. `false` adds `\"{label}: determination is false: <rationale>\"`.\n- Each evidence file is validated on its own, and the other checks still run. Those are the text check, schema and key checks, `validate_dependencies` and `validate_input` for stale or malformed inputs. FIXME therefore excuses nothing else.\n- The `true` and `FIXME` acceptance paths are tested:\n  - `tests/outcomes.rs::fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` accepts `FIXME` with an issue number and with free-text content.\n  - `tests/commands.rs::fixme_fixture` accepts `FIXME` for a requirement and an example.\n  - `tests/outcomes.rs::fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` accepts a `FIXME` example without a `{test}` reference.\n- The `false` failure is tested in `src/evidence.rs::collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors`, which asserts `\"determination is false\"`. `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` asserts the same message.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs::fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` shows that FIXME does not excuse stale inputs or uncovered references.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. **Rationale reporting is not asserted.** The requirement says a false determination must be \"reported with its rationale\". The implementation appends the trimmed rationale to the message. No test checks that it appears.\n   - The tests I read assert only the substring `\"determination is false\"`, never the rationale text.\n   - In the evidence.rs test, the fixture rationale `\"Work remains.\"` is never checked.\n   - The `status`/`info` tests in `tests/commands.rs` also check only the substring.\n   - The authoring tests that check rationales concern CLI output of the `author` command, not validation errors.\n2. **Per-definition independence is not tested.** The requirement says a false determination must not fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. Nothing under `requirements.ci.determination` verifies that.\n   - No test pairs one false record with valid dependents, citers or implementers and asserts that only the false one errors.\n   - The `status` test comes closest, since `pending` is false and `ready` is valid. But it is not marked as covering this requirement, and it does not assert a clean validation report for `ready`.\n   - Independence holds in the implementation because validation runs per file. That is a structural property, not a tested one.\n\nNeither gap is acknowledged by a `FIXME` in source or tests, so `FIXME` is not applicable. The rationale assertion and an independence assertion would close the gaps.",
  "inputs": [
